<title>USA: BOI - Short-term dollar move not greatly significant.</title>
<headline>BOI - Short-term dollar move not greatly significant.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Italy Governor Antonio Fazio said Monday that short-term movements of the dollar and other currencies are not greatly significant and must be seen within a longer timeframe.</p>
<p>&quot;We must look at them within a longertime frame, within weeks,&quot; Fazio told reporters asking him whether the dollar's recent rise makes a trend.</p>
<p>&quot;These dollar and foreign exchange moves are not of great significance. They must always be looked at in terms at least of weeks,&quot; Fazio said entering the G-10 meeting this morning.</p>
</text>
